---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="Privacy: What we do (and don't do) with your data" description="ShopVirge only stores what you share. We don't sell your data and we only use Google Analytics to measure visitor numbers." lang="en">
  <section class="hero text-white py-24 md:py-32">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-5xl">
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-white/60 mb-4">Privacy</p>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-extrabold mb-6 leading-[1.1] tracking-tight">What we do (and don't do) with your data</h1>
        <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-white/85 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
          Short and to the point. No legalese, no dark patterns.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-20 md:py-28">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-5xl prose prose-lg">
        <h2>What we store</h2>
        <p>
          We only store information that <strong>you actively share with us</strong>. That means:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Contact form submissions (name, email, phone, message, anything else you type in).</li>
          <li>Account and product data you enter into your ShopVirge shop, if you are a customer.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          On top of that, we use Google Analytics to measure, in aggregate, how many people visit the site and which
          pages are popular. We don't fingerprint your browser and we don't enrich your data with third-party sources.
        </p>

        <h2>Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          We use <strong>Google Analytics</strong> to understand how many visitors we get and which pages work best.
          To do this, Google sets a cookie and processes data such as your (anonymized) IP address, browser, and the
          pages you view. We use this purely to improve the site, not to identify you personally or to track you for
          advertising.
        </p>

        <h2>What we don't do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>We don't sell your data.</strong> Not to advertisers, not to brokers, not to anyone.</li>
          <li><strong>We don't use analytics for advertising.</strong> We don't link your visit to ad profiles, and we run no Facebook pixel or session replay.</li>
          <li><strong>We don't enrich your data.</strong> We don't combine what you share with outside data sources to build a profile of you.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How we use what you share</h2>
        <p>
          When you fill in the contact form or request a demo, the message is delivered to our team so we can reply
          to you. We keep it only as long as we need it for that conversation and any follow-up.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you become a customer, the data inside your shop (products, translations, orders) is used to operate
          your shop and nothing else. You can export everything at any time, and you can ask us to delete it.
        </p>

        <h2>Third parties we do rely on</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Formspree</strong> handles delivery of contact form submissions to our inbox.</li>
          <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> measures visitor numbers and which pages are popular.</li>
          <li><strong>Google Maps</strong> embeds the map on our contact page. The map only loads when you visit that page.</li>
          <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> hosts this website.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Each of these sees what is strictly needed to do their job (a form submission, a map tile request, a page
          request). None of them get a profile of who you are or what you do across the rest of the web.
        </p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>
          Under the GDPR you can ask us at any time what data we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to
          delete it. <a href={`${base}en/contact/`}>Get in touch</a> and we'll take care of it.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this statement</h2>
        <p>
          If we ever change how we handle data, we update this page first.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
